Relevant columns and their possible purposes for this task
-----------------------------------------------------------
`reference_name` : chromosome identifier – filter to chromosome ‘X’.

`start`           : genomic coordinate – apply the two exclusion windows.

`alternate_bases` : makes sure we are looking at true SNPs (single alt base).

`call`            : ARRAY of per‑sample genotype information – must be flattened.

`call.call_set_name` : sample ID to be reported.

`call.genotype`   : ARRAY<INT64> with the observed alleles – use to classify  
                    homo‑ref / homo‑alt / het and to check “callable” sites  
                    (ARRAY_LENGTH(genotype) > 0).

Conditions that will be used
----------------------------
• `reference_name = 'X'`  
• `start NOT BETWEEN 59999 AND 2699519`  
• `start NOT BETWEEN 154931042 AND 155260559`  
• `ARRAY_LENGTH(call.genotype) > 0`  
• A “true” SNP → `ARRAY_LENGTH(alternate_bases) = 1  
  AND LENGTH(reference_bases) = 1  
  AND LENGTH(alternate_bases[OFFSET(0)]) = 1`

